From: Cubewood <330162352+Cubewood@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:43:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Lane forks: a branch off the outer lanes gets an AI lead-in
 piece, so the AI settles on it near the fork

Where a one-way way's lanes split between one-way branches, a branch whose lanes lie off its own line at the fork gets its AI path in two pieces: a short lead-in from the fork, 0.15 m wider each side, then the rest at the branch's driving width. map.lua keeps the lead-in's end node (an end node while it loads and first thins the roads; the step in radius keeps the two ends apart in its first merge), so the navgraph has a node there and the AI is on the branch's line within a few metres, not over the whole first edge of a straight branch (50 m). The lead-in ends past the approach's radius and clear of the other branches' lines.

